on: list","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":303},{"base":"H8432","lemma":"תָּ֫וֶךְ","tr":"ta·vekh","gloss":"midst","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":418}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":25,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"Remember what the Amalekites did to you along your way from Egypt,","from":2},{"book":"DEU","chapter":25,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"When the LORD your God gives you rest from the enemies around you in the land that He is giving you to possess as an inheritance, you are to blot out the memory of Amalek from under heaven. Do not forget!","from":2},{"book":"EXO","chapter":17,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"After this, the Amalekites came and attacked the Israelites at Rephidim.","from":2},{"book":"EXO","chapter":17,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"“Indeed,” he said, “a hand was lifted up toward the throne of the LORD. The LORD will war against Amalek from generation to generation.”","from":2},{"book":"NUM","chapter":24,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Then Balaam saw Amalek and lifted up an oracle, saying: “Amalek was first among the nations, but his end is destruction.”","from":2},{"book":"JDG","chapter":1,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Now the descendants of Mosesʼ father-in-law, the Kenite, went up with the men of Judah from the City of Palms to the Wilderness of Judah in the Negev near Arad. They went to live among the people.","from":6},{"book":"1SA","chapter":9,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"“At this time tomorrow I will send you a man from the land of Benjamin, and you are to anoint him ruler over My people Israel; he will save them from the hand of the Philistines. For I have looked upon My people, because their cry has come to Me.”","from":1},{"book":"GEN","chapter":16,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now the angel of the Lordfound Hagar by a spring of water in the desert—the spring along the road to Shur.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"10-15":{"people":[{"id":"samuel-h8050g","name":"Samuel","kind":"person","brief":"Prophet and Judge","count":5,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"saul-h7586g","name":"Saul","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel,","count":4,"firstVerse":11}],"places":[{"id":"carmel-h3760g","name":"Carmel","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"gilgal-h1537g","name":"Gilgal","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"amalek-h6002g","name":"Amalek","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":15}],"words":[{"base":"H8050","lemma":"שְׁמוּאֵל","tr":"she·mu·el","gloss":"Samuel","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":140},{"base":"H7586","lemma":"שָׁאוּל","tr":"sha·ul","gloss":"Saul","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":406},{"base":"H1241","lemma":"בָּקָר","tr":"ba·qar","gloss":"cattle","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":183},{"base":"H6629","lemma":"צֹאן","tr":"tson","gloss":"flock","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":274},{"base":"H6963","lemma":"קוֹל","tr":"qol","gloss":"voice","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":506},{"base":"H4315","lemma":"מֵיטָב","tr":"me·tav","gloss":"best","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H6965","lemma":"קָמָי","tr":"qa·may","gloss":"(Leb)-kamai","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":628},{"base":"H3148","lemma":"יוֹתֵר","tr":"yo·ter","gloss":"advantage","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H6003","lemma":"עֲמָלֵקִי","tr":"a·ma·le·qi","gloss":"Amalekite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H3760","lemma":"כַּרְמֶל","tr":"kar·mel","gloss":"Carmel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":22}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1SA","chapter":13,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"“You have acted foolishly,” Samuel declared. “You have not kept the command that the LORD your God gave you; if you had, the LORD would have established your kingdom over Israel for all time.","from":11},{"book":"GEN","chapter":6,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"And the Lordregretted that He had made man on the earth, and He was grieved in His heart.","from":11},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":55,"verseEnd":55,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Maon, Carmel, Ziph, Juttah,","from":12},{"book":"2SA","chapter":24,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"But when the angel stretched out his hand to destroy Jerusalem, the LORD relented from the calamity and said to the angel who was destroying the people, “Enough! Withdraw your hand now!” At that time the angel of the LORD was by the threshing floor of Araunah the Jebusite.","from":11},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":136,"verseEnd":136,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"My eyes shed streams of tears because Your law is not obeyed.","from":11},{"book":"GEN","chapter":3,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the man answered, “The woman whom You gave me, she gave me fruit from the tree, and I ate it.”","from":13},{"book":"GEN","chapter":3,"verse":12,"verseEnd":13,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the man answered, “The woman whom You gave me, she gave me fruit from the tree, and I ate it.” Then the LordGod said to the woman, “What is this you have done?” “The serpent deceived me,” she replied, “and I ate.”","from":15},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"and he blessed Abram and said: “Blessed be Abram by God Most High, Creator of heaven and earth,","from":13}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"16-23":{"people":[{"id":"samuel-h8050g","name":"Samuel","kind":"person","brief":"Prophet and Judge","count":4,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"saul-h7586g","name":"Saul","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel,","count":2,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"agag-h0090h","name":"Agag","kind":"person","brief":"Amalakite king","count":1,"firstVerse":20}],"places":[{"id":"amalek-h6002g","name":"Amalek","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":2,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"gilgal-h1537g","name":"Gilgal","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21}],"words":[{"base":"H8050","lemma":"שְׁמוּאֵל","tr":"she·mu·el","gloss":"Samuel","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":140},{"base":"H6002","lemma":"עֲמָלֵק","tr":"a·ma·leq","gloss":"Amalek","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":39},{"base":"H8085","lemma":"שָׁמַע","tr":"sha·ma","gloss":"to hear: hear","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":1159},{"base":"H6963","lemma":"קוֹל","tr":"qol","gloss":"voice","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":506},{"base":"H2763","lemma":"חָרַם","tr":"cha·ram","gloss":"to devote","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":52},{"base":"H7998","lemma":"שָׁלָל","tr":"sha·lal","gloss":"spoil","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":73},{"base":"H3988","lemma":"מָאַס","tr":"ma·as","gloss":"to reject","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":76},{"base":"H2077","lemma":"זֶ֫בַח","tr":"ze·vach","gloss":"sacrifice","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":162},{"base":"H7586","lemma":"שָׁאוּל","tr":"sha·ul","gloss":"Saul","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":406},{"base":"H5860","lemma":"עִיט","tr":"it","gloss":"to scream","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"HOS","chapter":6,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":408,"source":"both","text":"For I desire mercy, not sacrifice, and the knowledge of God rather than burnt offerings.","from":22},{"book":"PSA","chapter":51,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":364,"source":"openbible","text":"For You do not delight in sacrifice, or I would bring it; You take no pleasure in burnt offerings.","from":22},{"book":"PSA","chapter":51,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":364,"source":"openbible","text":"The sacrifices of God are a broken spirit; a broken and a contrite heart, O God, You will not despise.","from":22},{"book":"PRO","chapter":21,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":339,"source":"both","text":"To do righteousness and justice is more desirable to the LORD than sacrifice.","from":22},{"book":"AMO","chapter":5,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":294,"source":"openbible","text":"“I hate, I despise your feasts! I cannot stand the stench of your solemn assemblies.","from":22},{"book":"AMO","chapter":5,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":294,"source":"openbible","text":"But let justice roll on like a river, and righteousness like an ever-flowing stream.","from":22},{"book":"MRK","chapter":12,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":283,"source":"both","text":"and to love Him with all your heart and with all your understanding and with all your strength, and to love your neighbor as yourself. This is more important than all burnt offerings and sacrifices.”","from":22},{"book":"MAT","chapter":9,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":253,"source":"both","text":"But go and learn what this means: ‘I desire mercy, not sacrifice.’ For I have not come to call the righteous, but sinners.”","from":22}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"24-31":{"people":[{"id":"samuel-h8050g","name":"Samuel","kind":"person","brief":"Prophet and Judge","count":5,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"saul-h7586g","name":"Saul","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel,","count":3,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":4,"firstVerse":26}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H8050","lemma":"שְׁמוּאֵל","tr":"she·mu·el","gloss":"Samuel","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":140},{"base":"H7586","lemma":"שָׁאוּל","tr":"sha·ul","gloss":"Saul","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":406},{"base":"H7812","lemma":"שָׁחָה","tr":"sha·chah","gloss":"to bow","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":172},{"base":"H7725","lemma":"שׁוּב","tr":"shuv","gloss":"to return: return","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":1057},{"base":"H7167","lemma":"קָרַע","tr":"qa·ra","gloss":"to tear","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":63},{"base":"H3988","lemma":"מָאַס","tr":"ma·as","gloss":"to reject","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":76},{"base":"H5162","lemma":"נָחַם","tr":"na·cham","gloss":"to be sorry: comfort","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":108},{"base":"H5973","lemma":"עִם","tr":"im","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1051},{"base":"H5048","lemma":"נֶ֫גֶד","tr":"ne·ged","gloss":"before","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":151},{"base":"H2398","lemma":"חָטָא","tr":"cha·ta","gloss":"to sin","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":238}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"NUM","chapter":23,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"God is not a man, that He should lie, or a son of man, that He should change His mind. Does He speak and not act? Does He promise and not fulfill?","from":29},{"book":"EZK","chapter":24,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"I, the LORD, have spoken; the time is coming, and I will act. I will not refrain or show pity, nor will I relent. I will judge you according to your ways and deeds,’ declares the Lord GOD.”","from":29},{"book":"TIT","chapter":1,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"in the hope of eternal life, which God, who cannot lie, promised before time began.","from":29},{"book":"2TI","chapter":2,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":15,"source":"both","text":"if we are faithless, He remains faithful, for He cannot deny Himself.","from":29},{"book":"HEB","chapter":6,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":15,"source":"both","text":"Thus by two unchangeable things in which it is impossible for God to lie, we who have fled to take hold of the hope set before us may be strongly encouraged.","from":29},{"book":"PSA","chapter":95,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"So I swore on oath in My anger, “They shall never enter My rest.”","from":29},{"book":"ISA","chapter":45,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Surely they will say of Me, ‘In the LORD alone are righteousness and strength.’” All who rage against Him will come to Him and be put to shame.","from":29},{"book":"JOL","chapter":3,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"The LORD will roar from Zion and raise His voice from Jerusalem; heaven and earth will tremble. But the LORD will be a refuge for His people, a stronghold for the people of Israel.","from":29}],"notes":[{"id":"1-sam-15-kingdom-torn","title":"The kingdom torn from Saul and from Solomon","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[]},"32-35":{"people":[{"id":"samuel-h8050g","name":"Samuel","kind":"person","brief":"Prophet and Judge","count":4,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"agag-h0090h","name":"Agag","kind":"person","brief":"Amalakite king","count":2,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"saul-h7586g","name":"Saul","kind":"person","brief":"King of Israel,","count":2,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":35}],"places":[{"id":"amalek-h6002g","name":"Amalek","kind":"place","brief":"In Edom","count":1,"firstVerse":32},{"id":"gilgal-h1537g","name":"Gilgal","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"gibeah-h1390h","name":"Gibeah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34},{"id":"mizpah-h4709g","name":"Mizpah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":34}],"words":[{"base":"H8050","lemma":"שְׁמוּאֵל","tr":"she·mu·el","gloss":"Samuel","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":140},{"base":"H0090","lemma":"אֲגָג","tr":"a·gag","gloss":"Agag","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":8},{"base":"H7586","lemma":"שָׁאוּל","tr":"sha·ul","gloss":"Saul","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":406},{"base":"H7921","lemma":"שָׁכֹל","tr":"sha·khol","gloss":"be bereaved","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":23},{"base":"H4194","lemma":"מָ֫וֶת","tr":"ma·vet","gloss":"death","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":155},{"base":"H4575","lemma":"מַעֲדַנּוֹת","tr":"ma·a·dan·nah","gloss":"bond","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H0802","lemma":"אִשָּׁה","tr":"ish·shah","gloss":"woman","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":781},{"base":"H0403","lemma":"אָכֵן","tr":"a·khen","gloss":"surely","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"H7414","lemma":"רָמָה","tr":"ra·mah","gloss":"Ramah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":36},{"base":"H4751","lemma":"מַר","tr":"mar","gloss":"bitter","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":37}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JDG","chapter":1,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Then Adoni-bezek said, “Seventy kings with their thumbs and big toes cut off have gathered the scraps under my table. As I have done to them, so God has repaid me.” And they brought him to Jerusalem, where he died.","from":33},{"book":"GEN","chapter":9,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Whoever sheds the blood of man, by man his blood will be shed; for in His own image God has made mankind.","from":33},{"book":"1SA","chapter":15,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"“I regret that I have made Saul king, for he has turned away from following Me and has not carried out My instructions.” And Samuel was distressed and cried out to the LORD all that night.","from":35},{"book":"1SA","chapter":19,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Then Saul stripped off his robes and also prophesied before Samuel. And he collapsed and lay naked all that day and night. That is why it is said, “Is Saul also among the prophets?”","from":35},{"book":"1SA","chapter":11,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"When the messengers came to Gibeah of Saul and relayed these words in the hearing of the people, they all wept aloud.","from":34},{"book":"GEN","chapter":6,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the Lordregretted that He had made man on the earth, and He was grieved in His heart.","from":35},{"book":"EXO","chapter":17,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"As long as Moses held up his hands, Israel prevailed; but when he lowered them, Amalek prevailed.","from":33},{"book":"NUM","chapter":14,"verse":45,"verseEnd":45,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Then the Amalekites and Canaanites who lived in that part of the hill country came down, attacked them, and routed them all the way to Hormah.","from":33}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}